[10600]="7006429A\n1\tExplore the sewers and confront Gárvadach\tLágsaith has begun her tale. With the heavy Angmarim presence in the sewers, Gárvadach cannot be far.\n2\tDefeat Gárvadach\tGárvadach has been discovered, and he is not happy about this untimely interruption.\n3\tExplore the sewers and confront Gárvadach (again)\tA heavily injured Gárvadach has fled deeper into the sewers.\n4\tDefeat Rádarríg\tGárvadach has met his demise at the hands of a... giant rat? It seems this \"king of rats\" will not stand for more trespassers!\n",
[10601]="70064EDF\n1\tTalk to Chiver Me Timbers\tBy completing this quest, you will automatically complete the Sagroth, Lair of Vermin, tiers 2 through 5 instance deeds or quests.\n",
[10602]="700642C1\n1\tEnter 'Sagroth, Lair of Vermin' on any difficulty\tUse the Instance Finder to enter 'Sagroth, Lair of Vermin' on any difficulty.\n2\tDestroy unidentifiable filth (total: 7)\tPiles of unidentifiable filth can be found in 'Sagroth, Lair of Vermin.' You should destroy them.\n3\tTalk to Avlath in Bail Avarc\tLágsaith has recounted, in excruciating detail, the disgusting filth she and her comrades encountered while in the sewers. You should tell Avlath in Bail Avarc.\n",
[10603]="700642C2\n1\tEnter 'Sagroth, Lair of Vermin' on any difficulty\tUse the Instance Finder to enter 'Sagroth, Lair of Vermin' on any difficulty.\n2\tCollect foul liquid samples (total: 5)\tFoul liquid can be found in 'Sagroth, Lair of Vermin.' You should collect some samples.\n3\tTalk to Náchtan in Bail Avarc\tLágsaith has described the foul liquid running through the sewers in vivid detail. You should tell Náchtan in Bail Avarc.\n",
[10604]="700642C0\n1\tEnter 'Sagroth, Lair of Vermin' on any difficulty\tUse the Instance Finder to enter 'Sagroth, Lair of Vermin' on any difficulty.\n2\tFind mapping points (total: 5)\tMapping points can be found in 'Sagroth, Lair of Vermin.' You should find them to complete the map of the sewers.\n3\tTalk to Aighrig in Bail Avarc\tThanks to Aighrig's map, Lágsaith's tale became a little less confusing to follow. You should return the map to Aighrig in Bail Avarc.\n",
[10605]="70044D5C\n1\tMeet Círgon at the Baths of Belecthor in the Fourth Circle\tThe Baths of Belecthor can be found in the northern part of the Fourth Circle. Círgon has asked you to join him at the Baths of Belecthor where he sails his model ships.\n2\tTalk to Círgon\tCírgon is standing at the Baths of Belecthor in the Fourth Circle. You have arrived at the Baths and should now talk to Círgon.\n3\tCollect Círgon's model ship of Umbar from his cart\tCírgon's cart can be found near the Baths of Belecthor in the Fourth Circle. Círgon has offered to let you place one of his ships into the Baths.\n4\tPlace the model ship of Umbar in the Baths' waters\tThe Baths of Belecthor can be found to the north in the Fourth Circle. You have picked up one of Círgon's ships and should now place it in the Baths.\n5\tTalk to Círgon\tCírgon is standing at the Baths of Belecthor in the Fourth Circle. You have set down the ship in the Baths and should now talk to Círgon.\n6\tTalk to Mílien\tMílien can be found outside her home in the Fourth Circle. Círgon has asked you to tell his mother that he will come home for supper once he finishes packing up his ships.\n",
[10606]="7002EA86\n1\tBurn salamander nests (total: 8)\tNests of the salamanders can be found in the Seething Mire. You should burn the nests of the salamanders, destroying as many as you can.\n2\tReturn to Higbald\tHigbald is at the gate of Langhold. You should return to Higbald now that you have set fire to many salamander nests, thus destroying several eggs.\n",
[10607]="70017597\n1\tReturn to Dithrik at the Foundations of Stone\030Acquire glow-worm glands (total: 6)\tThe Water Works are far to the south-west of the Foundations of Stone in Moria. You should slay many crawlers in the Water Works and collect their pungent glands. When you have acquired enough, you should return to Dithrik at the Foundations of Stone.\n",
[10608]="7004E148\n1\tComplete 'Fun at the Faire (Intro)'\tEvery day there is something to do during the Farmers Faire Festival. Come and join everyone and participate in many Farmers Faire activities for four days!\n2\tComplete 'Fun at the Faire (Intermediate)'\tEvery day there is something to do during the Farmers Faire Festival. Come and join everyone and participate in many Farmers Faire activities for four days!\n3\tComplete 'Fun at the Faire (Final)'\tEvery day there is something to do during the Farmers Faire Festival. Come and join everyone and participate in many Farmers Faire activities for four days!\n4\tTalk to Campanula Chubb\tCampanula Chubb can be found near the Party Tree in the Shire. You should talk to Campanula Chubb.\n",
[10609]="700080F3\n1\tBring the wheel back to [see journal]\030Collect the cart wheel\tThe broken waggons were dragged off by the Orcs to their camp outside of Nan Wathren. Some of the farmers, while escaping from the Orcs, were waylaid and their waggons were ruined. Mattie hopes that among the wreckage of the farmers' waggons you will find a wheel that he can use to fix his cart.\n",
[10610]="700346A2\n1\tCollect armour from Warg-riders (0/4)\tThe Warg-riders have captured Edsig's Farm and have converted it into a White Hand outpost. There are many Warg-riders patrolling the edges of their new outpost.\n2\tCollect armour from Warg-riders (total: 4)\tWarg-riders are keeping watch on the road, and the Fallows will not be safe while they ride unchecked.\n3\tReturn to Oter\tOter awaits your return to Thrymm's Farm, and will be eager to accept the scrap metal you have collected for him.\n",
[10611]="7006BF06\n1\tSpeak with Grove Elder Thórvilon and learn more of Vartúlin\tSpeak with Grove Elder Thórvilon and ascertain what is troubling him.\n2\tSpeak with Grove-tender Ulthral in Vartúlin about Milingor's poultice\tSpeak with Grove-tender Ulthral about a poultice for Thórvilon's wife, Milingor. She can be found on the higher level of Vartúlin, near the bridge.\n3\tSpeak with Milingor in her Veróth\tSpeak with Milingor, Thórvilon's wife, in her Veróth across the bridge from Thórvilon in Vartúlin.\n4\tPrune dead Sarláshi limbs from Milingor's Veróth (total: 3)\tPrune dead Sarláshi limbs from Milingor's Veróth.\n5\tSpeak once more with Grove Elder Thórvilon\tSpeak once more with Grove Elder Thórvilon at the edge of Vartúlin.\n6\tSpeak with Avadhril in Vartúlin\tSpeak with Avadhril to ascertain the details of contacting Usakâr the Hermit.\n7\tPick up oranges from under dying orange trees (total: 5)\tGo to the grove Avadhril mentioned east of Vartúlin and obtain some oranges for Usakâr.\n8\tFind Dag Usakâra, Usakâr's home east of Vartúlin\tFind Dag Usakâra, Usakâr's home. Avadhril mentioned it was east of Vartúlin, where the mountain ridge meets an open meadow.\n9\tSpeak with Usakâr and offer him the oranges\tSpeak with Usakâr and offer him the oranges.\n",
[10612]="7006BF05\n1\tSpeak with Usakâr at Dag Usakâra to mark your map\tSpeak with Usakâr and he will mark your map with the route to Cúridwan's home.\n2\tFind your way to the first point Usakâr has marked\tFind your way to the first point Usakâr has marked on your map.\n3\tFind your way to the second point Usakâr has marked\tFind your way to the second point Usakâr has marked on your map.\n4\tFind your way to the third point Usakâr has marked\tFind your way to the third point Usakâr has marked on your map.\n5\tSpeak with Usakâr at the mouth of the cave\tSpeak with Usakâr at the mouth of the cave.\n",
[10613]="7006BF04\n1\tSpeak with Usakâr by the cave door\tSpeak with Usakâr by the cave door.\n2\tGo through the cave entrance and enter Kûgrun\tGo through the cave entrance and enter Kûgrun, home of Cúridwan.\n3\tSpeak with Cúridwan, the Golden Maiden by her home\tSpeak with Cúridwan, the Golden Maiden by her cottage.\n4\tAsk Cúridwan about the ingredients necessary for the salve\tAsk Cúridwan about the ingredients necessary for the salve.\n5\tSpeak with Usakâr in Kûgrun\tSpeak with Usakâr in Kûgrun.\n6\tThank Cúridwan for her aid in the Kintai's plight\tThank Cúridwan for her aid in the Kintai's plight.\n7\tGather bog flowers from the marsh at Zahûmakh (total: 10)\030Gather bark from marsh-striders at Zahûmakh (total: 6)\030Gather wild berries from Dûlagig (total: 8)\030Gather scorpion venom from Dûlagig (total: 12)\tGather ingredients for Cúridwan: marsh-strider bark and bog flowers from the marsh at Zahûmakh to the east of Kûgrun, scorpion venom and berries from Dûlagig to the north of Kûgrun.\n8\tReturn to Cúridwan in Kûgrun with the ingredients you've gathered\tReturn to Cúridwan in Kûgrun with the ingredients you've gathered.\n",
[10614]="7006BF03\n1\tDestroy Ordâkhai founding stones at Ghât Lor (total: 3)\tCuridwan has tasked you with destroying Ordâkhai founding stones at Ghât Lor. Ghât Lor can be found far to the east of Kûgrun.\n2\tReturn to Cúridwan in Kûgrun\tReturn to Cúridwan in Kûgrun.\n3\tTake Cúridwan's salve\tTake Cúridwan's salve.\n4\tUse the salve on the river to heal Vartúlin\tUse the first phial of salve on the river behind Cúridwan's cottage to heal Vartúlin.\n5\tSpeak with Cúridwan before you leave\tSpeak with Cúridwan before you leave.\n6\tSpeak with Usakâr in Kûgrun\tSpeak with Usakâr in Kûgrun.\n",
[10615]="7006BF02\n1\tSpeak with Usakâr when you are ready to go\tSpeak with Usakâr to return to Vartúlin.\n2\tUse Cúridwan's salve to heal areas around Vartúlin (total: 8)\tUse Cúridwan's salve to heal areas afflicted with the Lâg Dávrit, the Pale Blight around Vartúlin.\n3\tSpeak with Thórvilon near the front of Vartúlin\tSpeak with Thórvilon near the edge of Vartúlin.\n",
[10616]="7006C21F\n1\tJoin Thórvilon near Milingor's Veróth\tThórvilon has gathered with some others around Milingor's Veróth. You should join them.\n2\tListen to Thórvilon\tListen to Thórvilon.\n3\tComfort Thórvilon\tComfort Thórvilon.\n4\tListen to Thórvilon and Usakâr's conversation\tListen to Thórvilon and Usakâr's conversation.\n5\tSpeak with Avadhril nearby\tSpeak with Avadhril nearby.\n",
[10617]="70022B49\n1\tDefeat Sambrog\tSambrog can be found in the greatest depths of the Great Barrow.\n",
[10618]="70026056\n1\tTake a sample from the first bag\tThe first bag of pipe-weed is on the table. You should get some pipe-weed from the first bag.\n2\tUse the pipe to sample the first bag of pipe-weed\tYou should use the pipe you were given to sample the pipe-weed.\n3\tTake a sample from the second bag\tThe second bag of pipe-weed is on the table. You should get some pipe-weed from the second bag.\n4\tUse the pipe to sample the second pipe-weed blend\tUse the pipe you were given to sample the second pouch of pipe-weed.\n5\tTake a sample from the third bag of pipe-weed\tThe third pouch is on the counter. You should take a sample of pipe-weed from the third pipe-weed pouch.\n6\tSample the third pipe-weed blend\tUse the pipe to sample the third pipe-weed blend.\n7\tReturn the pipe to Blossom Gamgee\tBlossom Gamgee is at the Pipe-weed House on the Northcotton Farm. Blossom Gamgee will want to know what you thought of the pipe-weed blends.\n",
[10619]="70070CD4\n1\tGather Pale Blight samples (total: 10)\tYour mission is to travel to Lhámuth and gather Pale Blight samples from the bog-lurkers there for the scholars of Sul Madásh.\n2\tDefeat the enraged Adagím thicket\tYour mission is to travel to Lhámuth and gather Pale Blight samples from the bog-lurkers there for the scholars of Sul Madásh.\n",
[10620]="7006AAD5\n1\tEnter Kheb Hanût\tKheb Hanût is in the north-western corner of Tâkhdar. The fence, Rashâm, has suggested you search for fallen coins in the black market of Kheb Hanût. He wants to pay a symbolic token of apology for the Ghôlkhas tomb-robbing.\n2\tLook for fallen coins in Kheb Hanût (total: 2)\tOld and forgotten coins will be found in Kheb Hanût, in the north-west of Tâkhdar. Rashâm would like you to collect some keepsake coins in the black market that no one will miss to represent a funerary token.\n3\tDrop the coins into the sea\tA good spot facing the sea is south of the Fisherfold in Umbar Baharbêl. Rashâm has asked you to drop old coins into the ocean by the Fisherfold in remembrance of a fallen hero whose tomb was robbed.\n4\tSpeak with Okhtâr Ghôlkhas\tOkhtâr Ghôlkhas is waiting inside Dâr Laja. You have paid your respects to the long-departed ancestor by dropping coins to the sea. Hopefully Rashâm has returned the Ghôlkhas armour by now. You should see if Okhtâr has news.\n",
[10621]="700266EC\n1\tAid Nimbellas with Robbers of Haudh Eärendur\030Aid Nimbellas with Entombed of Haudh Eärendur\030Aid Maladan with Kergrim of Haudh Valandur\030Aid Maladan with Valandur's Sceptre\030Aid Nethrandir with Ransackers of Haudh Arantar\030Aid Nethrandir with Arantar's Ring\030Aid Rodlam with Searchers of Haudh Eldacar\030Aid Rodlam with Orders of the Iron Crown\tThere is much to do within the open tombs of the Way of Kings.\n2\tTalk to Nimbellas in the Way of Kings\tNimbellas is at the Ranger-camp in the Way of Kings. Nimbellas will want to discuss the work done within the open crypts in the Way of Kings.\n",
[10622]="70068BB3\n1\tCollect sand from the spider-haunted ruins east of the city\030Collect sand to the west of one of the farms outside the city\030Collect sand from the hills north-east of the farms outside the city\030Collect sand south-east of the farms outside the city, near the river\tCharzâd asked you to collect sand from several different locations outside the city.\n2\tBring the sand you collected to Charzâd by the old observatory\tCharzâd is by the old observatory above the city, waiting for you to return to her with your discoveries.\n",
[10623]="70025951\n1\tCollect white sand (total: 15)\tWhite sand can be found in the Sand Marshes north of Dwaling. Mundaric Sandheaver has asked you to gather some white sand for him.\n2\tBring the white sand to Mundaric Sandheaver in Dwaling\tMundaric Sandheaver is at Hob Hillbrow's home at the Bullroarer's Sward in Dwaling, south of the Sand-marshes. You should return to Mundaric Sandheaver with the white sand.\n",
[10624]="70063FBF\n1\tPick up the summoning horn and call Forba to your side\tYou have entered the Poison Gardens of Carn Dûm, Sant Lhoer. You should use the nearby summoning horn to call an ally, Forba, to your side.\n2\tSearch for Oganuin within Sant Lhoer\tYou should explore Sant Lhoer and look for the sorceress Oganuin. NOTE: You can use the 'Call Forba' skill to call Forba to your side in Sant Lhoer.\n3\tDefeat Tarkka-oka and Cráthair\tWithin Sant Lhoer you have come across an Angmarim sorcerer, Cráthair, and his companion, the Jorthkyn Tarkka-oka. The latter is like nothing you have ever seen before. This must be one of Oganuin's foul experiments! You should defeat the pair. NOTE: You can use the 'Call Forba' skill to call Forba to your side in Sant Lhoer.\n4\tUnlock the North Gate\tWhen you defeated Tarkka-oka and Cráthair, you acquired the key to the North Gate. You should unlock the North Gate and continue on. NOTE: You can use the 'Call Forba' skill to call Forba to your side in Sant Lhoer.\n5\tDefeat Oganuin\tYou stand before Bâr Heledh, the Glass House of Carn Dûm. Within its metal and glass walls the sorceress Oganuin practices her fell crafts, creating abominations and twisting living things towards unnatural ends. You should defeat Oganuin. NOTE: You can use the 'Call Forba' skill to call Forba to your side in Sant Lhoer.\n",
})
